
Simple San Simon Functional Web Browser
=======================================

It is a computer desktop program for rendering web pages.
One nice thing is that it is written with Haskell, a purely funcional programming language.
It supports a generic markup language (like ~ html or xhtml or xml) and part of CSS.

To install
----------

	cabal install

We have a configuration directory ('config' directory) that should be placed
at your home directory: '~/.3SFWebBrowser/'.  Cabal creates it automatically.

You will need to edit '~/.3SFWebBrowser/dbf' and setup the proper path for
'User_Agent_Stylesheet' which is located at the same directory.

Note: the GUI is being migrated from wxHaskell to haskell-gi (GTK 4).
For now only the Boxer GUI (3sfboxer) is built; the web browser
executable (3sfwbrowser) is disabled in the cabal file.


Boxer GUI (3sfboxer)
--------------------

3sfboxer shows the box tree of the formatting structure of a page, and the
CSS properties (specified, computed, used and actual values) of each box.

Requirements:

  * GHC (tested with 9.10.3) and cabal-install (tested with 3.12)
  * GTK 4, GObject Introspection, libgd and libcurl, with their development
    files. On Debian/Ubuntu:

	sudo apt install pkg-config libgtk-4-dev libgirepository1.0-dev libgd-dev libcurl4-openssl-dev

uuagc (the attribute grammar compiler) and the haskell-gi bindings are
fetched and built by cabal; the first build takes a while.

To build, from the root of the repository:

	cabal update
	cabal build 3sfboxer

To start it, also from the root of the repository (it reads
'./config/html4.css'):

	cabal run 3sfboxer

Type a URL (for example file:///<path to the repository>/examples/test1.html,
which is the default) and press Enter or the "Dibujar" button. Click a box
to see its properties.


For more information
--------------------

